-- title:
--   The selected triple polynomial is an allowed descendant
-- statement:
--   For a matroid $N$ on a finite ambient type $E$, define the homogenized rank-weight polynomial
--   $$T_{N,q}(z_0,(z_e)_{e\in E})=\sum_{A\subseteq E}(q^{r_N(A)})^{-1}z_0^{|E|-|A|}\prod_{e\in A}z_e,$$
--   where $r_N(A)$ is the natural finite rank. The reciprocal is the total rational inverse, so $0^{-1}=0$.
--
--   For matroids $M_1,M_2$ on $[n]$, form $N=M_1\oplus M_2^*$ on paired labels, using label $0$ for $M_1$ and label $1$ for $M_2^*$. Let $F$ result from $\partial_{z_0}^{\,n}T_{N,q}$ by setting $z_0=0$ and identifying both labels at pair $u$ with $z_u$. For indices $i,j,k$, extract exponent one at every pair outside $\{i,j,k\}$ by differentiating once and setting that variable to zero, in increasing index order. Differentiate the result at $k$, substitute $z_u\mapsto\mathbf1_{u=i}x_0+\mathbf1_{u=j}x_1+\mathbf1_{u=k}x_2$, and multiply by $q^n/n!$. Denote the result by $G_{ijk}$. For every natural $n$, matroids $M_1,M_2$ on $[n]$, positive rational $q$, and indices $i,j,k$,
--
--   $$G_{ijk}\in\operatorname{Desc}(T_{N,q}),$$
--
--   where descendants are obtained by finitely many coordinate derivatives, linear substitutions with nonnegative rational coefficients, and multiplication by nonnegative rational scalars. No distinctness assumption on $i,j,k$ is needed for this membership claim.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/DefectPartitionQuadraticConstruction.lean#L85-L122

